probably the most common question that  I'm asked as a professor at Hillsdale is  what happened to my country you know  when they poll Americans they find that  a vast majority don't think the world is  going to be a better place for their own  children  in this course we're going to look at  who the mid-century liberals were and  the changes that they introduced into  American society we're also going to  look at the radicals the  counter-culturalists of the 1960s and  the changes that remain with us today  we're going to look at the group called  The neoliberals and the formation of an  oligarchy in the American regime in the  1980s and the 1990s and finally we'll  see how those radicals in the 60s made  peace with those neoliberal oligarchs in  the great awokening and Barack Obama's  second term and the threat that it poses  to Republican Liberties for us today  these movements are promising to strip  away all of the rights and the freedoms  that give life happiness and meaning and  purpose I don't think people understand  the source of most current ideologies  and what this course is going to show us  is where they originated and how they  took control of our society you'll see  the changes that have taken place in  America the ideas that are responsible  for those changes and how we as  Americans can challenge those ideas and  reclaim our American Heritage this is  our course on the American left  let's begin  [Music]
 

